---
// How to use the Theme Builder's color controls, shown under "Create theme
// groups" in the Builder Guide (src/pages/website-builder/index.astro).
---

<p>
  Assign palette colors to each area’s canvas, text, buttons, links, icons, and
  interactive states. Changes only affect the sample page.
</p>
<p>
  Click a heading, paragraph, button, menu item, card, or social icon in the
  preview to center and highlight its color control. Click the section
  background to edit its border.
</p>
<p>
  Choose the editing area in the floating Style Picker. Sections 1–6 use the
  first–sixth token groups. “Theme default” follows your existing light/dark
  theme. Global (the CTA colors), Header, and Footer are sitewide: they are
  saved to sitewide.css rather than a theme group. Choose Page canvas to edit
  page-wide brand colors. The interactive group includes button hover, focus,
  and active states; link, visited, hover, focus, and active states; and icon
  colors for each area.
</p>
